# ext4: correct behavior under errors=remount-ro mode
# Upstream series (ext4, merged in v6.15-rc1): EXT4_FLAGS_SHUTDOWN was being set for
# errors=remount-ro, which blocks reads as well as writes. These five patches
# introduce EXT4_FLAGS_EMERGENCY_RO and use it for that case, so reads keep
# working while writes are refused.
# They are one dependent set and must stay in this order: 0002 defines the new
# flag, 0003/0004 add the ext4_emergency_state() checks that make it effective,
# and only then does 0005 switch the error path over to it.
